{"format":1,"seq":84,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since message_end can't directly update the component, I'm checking whether mutating the original block's arguments object in place would work instead of maintaining a separate map — it depends on whether the streaming component holds a reference to that same arguments object.\n\nMutation feels fragile though since the test expects a fresh empty object for parse failures, and the component's args may actually be a different object instance due to streaming parse behavior. I'll stick with the map approach, and simplify by replacing display-input.ts with a small helper inside typescript.ts that checks if recovered code exists and the args lack a code field, removing displayInputResolved from the renderer files and dropping the pi-ai peer dependency change. I'm also planning to drop the partial-streaming display behavior change and its associated coercion tests.\n\nSeveral test cases around caching and persisted raw calls become unnecessary since plain displayArguments has no caching logic, so those assertions become trivially true — I'll remove them. For the invalid-options test cases, I'm checking whether invalid values like saveOnly: \"yes\" still render correctly in the source comment versus getting pulled into the result view's inputs.\n\nFor raw-call-recovery, I'm considering minor cleanup like simplifying the recover function's return shape, but most of the guard logic should stay as-is since it's not central to this fix.\n\nFor the test suite, the live test spawns real Pi multiple times which is heavy — I'm thinking of trimming it down to just the essential cases (plain source, options, malformed) since that's what actually validates the core claim that message_end replacement affects execution, and dropping the redundant save-coercion case.\n\nI'm also debating whether to keep the serializer test that checks custom_tool_call replay through internal dist paths — it's fragile against Pi upgrades but it directly verifies the actual mechanism behind context repair, so I'll keep it despite the brittleness.\n\nBefore touching any tests, I should follow the pit-test-audit skill's instructions, reread the current test file contents from the diff, and check how renderToolResult is defined in the extension-fixture helpers.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01E1z8moXod8QUJnNHyfUVN9","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Load pit-test-audit skill and check isProgramExpression for empty source\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { read, search } }) => {\n  const [s, p] = await Promise.all([\n    read(\".pi/skills/pit-test-audit/SKILL.md\", { format: \"raw\" }),\n    search(\"export function isProgramExpression\", { path: \"src/functions/source.ts\", contextLines: 10 }),\n  ]);\n  return { s: s.content.slice(0, 9000), p: p.matches.map((m) => [...m.before, m, ...m.after].map((l) => l.text).join(\"\\n\")) };\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1978,"cacheRead":57585,"cacheWrite":1781,"totalTokens":61346,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1720},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1795130915611,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_eelgvwkqcb2hlygvkpjrfmvxehrbesmtlk5ndyby7zjbcdvisgaa","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":22496,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"kind":"pi.assistant","id":37,"conversationId":1,"byTaskId":36}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":36,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.generation","version":2,"input":{},"background":false,"abortRequested":false,"state":{"status":"waiting","checkpoint":{"phase":"tools","assistant":37,"tools":[38],"pending":[]},"on":[38],"policy":"allSettled"},"startedAt":1795130915582}},{"type":"task","value":{"id":38,"conversationId":1,"kind":"pi.tool","version":3,"input":{"kin